This API route (Nodemailer POST handler) cannot exist in a static export build —
Next.js `output: 'export'` fails the build on any non-GET route handler, since
there's no Node server on Hostinger shared hosting to run it.

The original route.ts has been removed. WelcomePopup.tsx now shows the discount
code directly on-screen instead of relying on a server to email it, and
optionally posts the lead to Web3Forms (see WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY in that file)
for a pure client-side, static-hosting-compatible notification.

If you later move to a host that runs Node (Vercel, Hostinger's Node tier, etc.)
you can restore the real route.ts from git history / backup and switch
WelcomePopup back to calling /api/send-discount.
